The aligned column is UNCHANGED at every preset -- the change is byte-neutral
on 64-aligned frames by construction (every edge branch is dead when both
has_rows and has_cols are true), and this is the measurement that says so
rather than the argument.

p5 did not move. Its 11 remaining partial-SB divergences are therefore a
DIFFERENT root from the one this fixed, not a weaker case of it; p5 is the last
preset before the funnel path changes shape, so that is where to look. Not
diagnosed here -- recorded so the next session does not assume the two are the
same problem.
